            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-102010",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gcc-toolset-15-gcc: gcc: gcc-toolset-16: gcc: Denial of Service via use-after-free in binary heap erase_if"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GCC. When an application calls the erase_if function on a binary heap priority queue in libstdc++, the library reallocates storage but fails to update its internal entry pointer. An attacker capable of triggering this operation can exploit this use-after-free condition, leading to a Denial of Service (DoS) via an application crash or potential memory corruption."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-102010",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-102010\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libstdc++6\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-102010](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-102010)\nA flaw was found in GCC. When an application calls the erase_if function on a binary heap priority queue in libstdc++, the library reallocates storage but fails to update its internal entry pointer. An attacker capable of triggering this operation can exploit this use-after-free condition, leading to a Denial of Service (DoS) via an application crash or potential memory corruption.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-102010**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libstdc++6||[CVE-2026-102010](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-102010)|\n\nA flaw was found in GCC. When an application calls the erase_if function on a binary heap priority queue in libstdc++, the library reallocates storage but fails to update its internal entry pointer. An attacker capable of triggering this operation can exploit this use-after-free condition, leading to a Denial of Service (DoS) via an application crash or potential memory corruption."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
