            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-95619",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gcc: libstdc++ integer overflow in `new` operator"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libstdc++. An integer overflow can occur when processing large inputs to the aligned operator new in the C++ library. This vulnerability could lead to an undersized memory allocation, potentially causing memory corruption or application instability."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-95619",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-95619\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libstdc++6\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-95619](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-95619)\nA flaw was found in libstdc++. An integer overflow can occur when processing large inputs to the aligned operator new in the C++ library. This vulnerability could lead to an undersized memory allocation, potentially causing memory corruption or application instability.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-95619**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libstdc++6||[CVE-2026-95619](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-95619)|\n\nA flaw was found in libstdc++. An integer overflow can occur when processing large inputs to the aligned operator new in the C++ library. This vulnerability could lead to an undersized memory allocation, potentially causing memory corruption or application instability."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
