            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-6368",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: glibc: Process abort due to invalid memory in wordexp"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling wordexp with WRDE_APPEND in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.43 can cause the interface to return invalid memory in the we_wordv member, which on subsequent calls to wordfree may abort the process."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-6368",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-6368\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-6368](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-6368)\nCalling wordexp with WRDE_APPEND in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.43 can cause the interface to return invalid memory in the we_wordv member, which on subsequent calls to wordfree may abort the process.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-6368**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libc6||[CVE-2026-6368](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-6368)|\n\nCalling wordexp with WRDE_APPEND in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.43 can cause the interface to return invalid memory in the we_wordv member, which on subsequent calls to wordfree may abort the process."
              },
              "properties": {
