            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-32822",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "hbs: Insertion of Sensitive Information into Externally-Accessible File or Directory and Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The npm hbs package is an Express view engine wrapper for Handlebars. Depending on usage, users of hbs may be vulnerable to a file disclosure vulnerability. There is currently no patch for this vulnerability. hbs mixes pure template data with engine configuration options through the Express render API. By overwriting internal configuration options a file disclosure vulnerability may be triggered in downstream applications. For an example PoC see the referenced GHSL-2021-020."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
