            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-113654",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sanitize-html: sanitize-html: HTML sanitization bypass via improper noscript tag handling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system, and sanitize-html provides a simple HTML sanitizer with a clear API. Prior to sanitize-html 2.18.0, a non-default nonTextTags configuration that includes noscript can end its discard region early when htmlparser2 emits an implied ancestor close inside noscript. Because scripting-enabled browsers treat noscript content as raw text while the parser does not model that mode, content intended to remain inert can survive sanitization and render; the issue does not generalize to every default nonTextTags element. This issue is fixed in sanitize-html 2.18.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-113654",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-113654\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: sanitize-html\nFixed Version: 2.18.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-113654](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-113654)\nApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system, and sanitize-html provides a simple HTML sanitizer with a clear API. Prior to sanitize-html 2.18.0, a non-default nonTextTags configuration that includes noscript can end its discard region early when htmlparser2 emits an implied ancestor close inside noscript. Because scripting-enabled browsers treat noscript content as raw text while the parser does not model that mode, content intended to remain inert can survive sanitization and render; the issue does not generalize to every default nonTextTags element. This issue is fixed in sanitize-html 2.18.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-113654**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|sanitize-html|2.18.0|[CVE-2026-113654](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-113654)|\n\nApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system, and sanitize-html provides a simple HTML sanitizer with a clear API. Prior to sanitize-html 2.18.0, a non-default nonTextTags configuration that includes noscript can end its discard region early when htmlparser2 emits an implied ancestor close inside noscript. Because scripting-enabled browsers treat noscript content as raw text while the parser does not model that mode, content intended to remain inert can survive sanitization and render; the issue does not generalize to every default nonTextTags element. This issue is fixed in sanitize-html 2.18.0."
              },
              "properties": {
