              "id": "CVE-2026-113661",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sanitize-html: sanitize-html: Cross-site scripting via unsafe meta refresh content attributes"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system, and sanitize-html provides a simple HTML sanitizer with a clear API. Prior to sanitize-html 2.18.0, a non-default configuration that allows meta refresh elements and their http-equiv and content attributes can retain unsafe script or redirect destinations embedded in the refresh content value. This issue is fixed in sanitize-html 2.18.0."
