                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-113661**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|sanitize-html|2.18.0|[CVE-2026-113661](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-113661)|\n\nApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system, and sanitize-html provides a simple HTML sanitizer with a clear API. Prior to sanitize-html 2.18.0, a non-default configuration that allows meta refresh elements and their http-equiv and content attributes can retain unsafe script or redirect destinations embedded in the refresh content value. This issue is fixed in sanitize-html 2.18.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.4,
