            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-63670",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ApostropheCMS: Mutation-XSS / allowedTags bypass via literal `\u003c/textarea/\u003e` solidus close"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system. Prior to 2.17.6, sanitizeHtml() can pass disallowed executable markup through packages/sanitize-html/index.js when textarea or xmp is included in allowedTags because a literal solidus after the raw-text end-tag name is treated as text by htmlparser2 and the ontext handler emits that content without escaping, while a browser parses the following img onerror markup as active HTML. This issue is fixed in version 2.17.6."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63670",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-63670\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: sanitize-html\nFixed Version: 2.17.6\nLink: [CVE-2026-63670](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63670)\nApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system. Prior to 2.17.6, sanitizeHtml() can pass disallowed executable markup through packages/sanitize-html/index.js when textarea or xmp is included in allowedTags because a literal solidus after the raw-text end-tag name is treated as text by htmlparser2 and the ontext handler emits that content without escaping, while a browser parses the following img onerror markup as active HTML. This issue is fixed in version 2.17.6.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-63670**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|sanitize-html|2.17.6|[CVE-2026-63670](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63670)|\n\nApostropheCMS is an open-source Node.js content management system. Prior to 2.17.6, sanitizeHtml() can pass disallowed executable markup through packages/sanitize-html/index.js when textarea or xmp is included in allowedTags because a literal solidus after the raw-text end-tag name is treated as text by htmlparser2 and the ontext handler emits that content without escaping, while a browser parses the following img onerror markup as active HTML. This issue is fixed in version 2.17.6."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
