            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59873",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "tar: node-tar: Denial of Service via crafted gzip bomb"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "node-tar is a tar archive manipulation library for Node.js. Prior to 7.5.19, node-tar does not enforce hard upper bounds on total decompressed data, entry counts, or decompression ratio in extraction and parsing paths such as src/extract.ts, allowing a small crafted gzip bomb to exhaust disk space and CPU. This issue is fixed in version 7.5.19."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59873",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59873\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: tar\nFixed Version: 7.5.19\nLink: [CVE-2026-59873](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59873)\nnode-tar is a tar archive manipulation library for Node.js. Prior to 7.5.19, node-tar does not enforce hard upper bounds on total decompressed data, entry counts, or decompression ratio in extraction and parsing paths such as src/extract.ts, allowing a small crafted gzip bomb to exhaust disk space and CPU. This issue is fixed in version 7.5.19.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59873**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|tar|7.5.19|[CVE-2026-59873](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59873)|\n\nnode-tar is a tar archive manipulation library for Node.js. Prior to 7.5.19, node-tar does not enforce hard upper bounds on total decompressed data, entry counts, or decompression ratio in extraction and parsing paths such as src/extract.ts, allowing a small crafted gzip bomb to exhaust disk space and CPU. This issue is fixed in version 7.5.19."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
