            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59875",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "node-tar: node-tar: Denial of Service via crafted archive with NUL bytes in metadata"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "node-tar is a tar archive manipulation library for Node.js. Prior to 7.5.17, node-tar does not strip NUL bytes from PAX path and linkpath records in src/pax.ts, allowing a crafted archive with values to reach fs.lstat or fs.open and terminate the process with an uncaught exception. This issue is fixed in version 7.5.17."
